class:: DualPulsarOS
summary:: A bandlimited pulsar oscillator with cross-phase modulation, phase increment distortion, and optional oversampling
categories:: UGens>Oscillator

DESCRIPTION::
DualPulsarOS is a bandlimited pulsar oscillator with cross-phase modulation, phase increment distortion, and optional oversampling. 
It supports up to 8 simultaneously active grains with internal voice allocation.

Sub-sample-accurate event scheduling of grains can be achieved by combining DualPulsarOS with SchedulerCycle or SchedulerBurst, 
which provide the necessary timing information (trigger, rate, and subsample offset).

Each grain consists of two cross-phase-modulated wavetable oscillators shaped by a Gaussian window. 
The oscillators modulate each other’s phase through a single-sample feedback loop, 
with independent modulation indices controlling the depth of each cross-modulation path. 
Each path includes a slope-tracking one-pole filter whose cutoff follows the modulator’s fundamental frequency 
and is scaled by the corresponding filter ratio. 
The wavetable oscillators are bandlimited via dynamic mipmapping and sinc interpolation.

Phase increment distortion redistributes the oscillator cycles within each grain via a cubic easing function, 
providing continuous per-grain pitch modulation over the duration of each grain.

Grains can be overlapped by dividing the scheduler rate by the desired overlap amount before passing it as the trigger frequency. 
An overlap of 1 means each grain lasts exactly one trigger period, while higher values produce longer, overlapping grains.

note::
High overlap values require more CPU as more grains are active simultaneously.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: trig
Trigger signal, for example derived from SchedulerCycle or SchedulerBurst.

ARGUMENT:: triggerFreq
Trigger frequency in Hz, for example derived from SchedulerCycle or SchedulerBurst.
Used by the internal voice allocator to calculate the grain duration.
Typically the scheduler rate divided by the overlap amount.

ARGUMENT:: subSampleOffset
Subsample offset for accurate grain timing, for example derived from SchedulerCycle or SchedulerBurst.

ARGUMENT:: oscFreq
Carrier oscillator frequency in Hz. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: modFreq
Modulator oscillator frequency in Hz. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: oscXmIndex
Cross-phase modulation depth received by osc from mod. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: modXmIndex
Cross-phase modulation depth received by mod from osc. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: oscXmFltRatio
Damping filter ratio for the cross-phase modulation path from mod to osc. 
Sets the filter cutoff as a multiple of the modulator's fundamental frequency (default: 1). 
Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: modXmFltRatio
Damping filter ratio for the cross-phase modulation path from osc to mod. 
Sets the filter cutoff as a multiple of the oscillator's fundamental frequency (default: 1). 
Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: oscWarp
Phase increment distortion for osc. Redistributes the osc cycles within each grain via a cubic easing function.
0.5 = linear (no effect), < 0.5 = cycles concentrated toward the grain start, > 0.5 = cycles concentrated toward the grain end.
Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: modWarp
Phase increment distortion for mod. Redistributes the mod cycles within each grain via a cubic easing function.
0.5 = linear (no effect), < 0.5 = cycles concentrated toward the grain start, > 0.5 = cycles concentrated toward the grain end.
Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: oscBuffer
Buffer containing carrier wavetable data (the size has to be a power-of-2).

ARGUMENT:: oscNumCycles
Number of cycles in the carrier wavetable buffer.

ARGUMENT:: oscCyclePos
Position within the carrier multi-cycle wavetable (0.0 to 1.0).

ARGUMENT:: modBuffer
Buffer containing modulator wavetable data (the size has to be a power-of-2).

ARGUMENT:: modNumCycles
Number of cycles in the modulator wavetable buffer.

ARGUMENT:: modCyclePos
Position within the modulator multi-cycle wavetable (0.0 to 1.0).

ARGUMENT:: envSkew
Skew of the gaussian window (0.0 to 1.0). At 0.5 the window is symmetric. Lower values shift the peak toward the grain start, higher values toward the grain end.

ARGUMENT:: envIndex
Shape index of the gaussian window (0.0 to 10.0). At 0 the window is a hanning window. Higher values narrow the gaussian peak.

ARGUMENT:: oversample
Oversampling factor: 0=1x, 1=2x, 2=4x, 3=8x, 4=16x.

returns:: Audio-rate UGen.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// load multi-cycle wavetable
(
t = Signal.sineFill(2048, [1], [0]);
u = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/((1..512)**2)*([1,0,-1,0]!128).flatten);
w = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/(1..512)*([1,0]!256).flatten);
x = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/(1..512));
v = t.addAll(u).addAll(w).addAll(x);
~oscBuf = Buffer.loadCollection(s, v);
~modBuf = Buffer.loadCollection(s, v);
)

// Basic cross-phase modulated pulsar
(
{
	var events, overlap, windowRate, sig;

	events = SchedulerCycle.ar(\tFreq.kr(100));

	overlap = \overlap.kr(4);
	windowRate = events[\rate] / max(0.001, overlap);

	sig = DualPulsarOS.ar(
		trig: events[\trigger],
		triggerFreq: windowRate,
		subSampleOffset: events[\subSampleOffset],
		oscFreq: \oscFreq.kr(440),
		modFreq: \modFreq.kr(440),
		oscXmIndex: \oscXmIndex.kr(1),
		modXmIndex: \modXmIndex.kr(0.5),
		oscXmFltRatio: 1,
		modXmFltRatio: 1,
		oscWarp: 0.5,
		modWarp: 0.5,
		oscBuffer: ~oscBuf,
		oscNumCycles: 4,
		oscCyclePos: 0,
		modBuffer: ~modBuf,
		modNumCycles: 4,
		modCyclePos: 0,
		envSkew: 0.5,
		envIndex: 0,
		oversample: 0,
	);

	sig = LeakDC.ar(sig);
	sig ! 2 * 0.1;
}.play;
)

// Phase increment distortion — non-linear pitch trajectories per grain
(
{
	var events, overlap, windowRate, sig;

	events = SchedulerCycle.ar(\tFreq.kr(5));

	overlap = \overlap.kr(1);
	windowRate = events[\rate] / max(0.001, overlap);

	sig = DualPulsarOS.ar(
		trig: events[\trigger],
		triggerFreq: windowRate,
		subSampleOffset: events[\subSampleOffset],
		oscFreq: 800,
		modFreq: 400,
		oscXmIndex: 1,
		modXmIndex: 0,
		oscWarp: \oscWarp.kr(0),
		modWarp: 0.5,
		oscBuffer: ~oscBuf,
		oscNumCycles: 4,
		oscCyclePos: 0,
		modBuffer: ~modBuf,
		modNumCycles: 4,
		modCyclePos: 0,
		envSkew: 0.5,
		envIndex: 0,
		oversample: 0,
	);

	sig = LeakDC.ar(sig);
	sig ! 2 * 0.3;
}.play;
)
::
